<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mount Morgan, Queensland</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mount Morgan is a town in central Queensland, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>, south-west of Rockhampton, which grew around one of the world's richest gold mines. Gold was found there in the early 1880s, and the Mount Morgan mine produced gold and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> for about a century, until the 1980s. Its profits helped the investor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-knox-darcy">William Knox D'Arcy</a> finance the oil search in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> that led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bp">Anglo-Persian Oil Company</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mount-morgan-queensland.jpg" alt="Mount Morgan, Queensland" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Heritage branch staff · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mount_Morgan_State_High_School_-_former_Technical_College_Building,_from_E_(2015).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
